__pycache__/
ALERT.md

# per-run health handoff: run_pipeline.py writes it, export_signal.py reads it
pipeline_status.json

# newslib.atomic_write_text stages here before os.replace. It cleans up on a
# normal exception, but a SIGKILL (cancelled runner, job time limit) cannot run
# any handler, so one can survive. Ignored so a half-written stage file can never
# be committed even if someone widens the workflow's `git add`.
*.tmp

# local knowledge-graph artifacts
graphify-out/

# The news database is a RELEASE ASSET, not a tracked file. It outgrew GitHub's
# 100 MiB per-file push limit (88.7 MiB on 2026-09-10, +1.6 MiB/day), and a
# rejected push stops EVERY committed artifact updating, silently. The pipeline
# fetches it from the `data` release at the start of each run and publishes it
# back at the end. See .github/workflows/pipeline.yml.
#
# Its ~933 committed versions stay in history (257 MiB packed) — untracking it
# going forward does not and need not rewrite that.
news.db
news-*.db
